Z||000001||KRMFiero||05-22-2001||07:04 AM||||Try replacing your horn,harazed relays they are under your passanger side dash||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||05-22-2001||07:51 PM||||Check for a bad ground.  There may be a common ground in those circuits, a bad ground jiggling car connects/disconnects.  Sorry to say electrical problems are the biggest pain in the butt.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||05-22-2001||07:57 PM||||I agree with Lar. chk for bad grounds. Horns grounded good, so it prob just no good. good time for some twin air horns.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||05-22-2001||09:34 PM||||Could be multiple problems.  My radio would intermittently stop working due -- I think -- to internal problems.  I replaced it with a known good stock unit, which works fine.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||05-22-2001||09:55 PM||||The horns are grounded through there mounting bracket, and tail lights are grounded at g400 at rhs rear of engine compartment. Fuses are also different. tail and bat fuse. I agree that it is now time for twin horns if you are hearing the horn relay click from rhs of instrument panel. The tail lights share the same ground as brake lights and turn signals and since you are not experiencing a problem with them I would say your problem is probably the headlight switch itself.  my thoughts||||reg||1
